{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963313-lodge-of-the-seven-pyres","id":963313,"title":"Lodge of the Seven Pyres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-04T11:53:31-07:00","id":963313,"title":"Lodge of the Seven Pyres","content":"I'm working on a Lodge that hunts Claimed. I will post it when it nears completion, but right now I want to ask about the sacred hunt. I came up with a couple different effects, one much more powerful than the other. With only a few Lodges in 2e form, there's not much to base off of right now, but I wanted to see what the gang thought. Here is the lesser one, which I'm leaning towards:<br /> <br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt allows your character to disrupt the prey spirit's protection from the host; by spending an Essence and successfully striking the Claimed (without causing damage), the Uratha causes the spirit to bleed a point of Essence per hour. This effect lasts for a number of hours equal to the Uratha's Primal Urge. In addition, during this time, the leaking Essence creates a trail of resonance that adds a one die bonus to attempt to track the Claimed. Multiple strikes will not increase the hemorrhaging of Essence, but will add to the length of time it is in effect.<br /> <br /> Here is the more powerful one:<br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt allows your character to disrupt the prey spirit's connection with the host; by spending an Essence and successfully striking the Claimed (without causing damage), the Uratha forces the spirit to spend double the amount of Essence for any use of Influence; in addition, any Dread Power costs a point of Essence to use actively (<i>eg.,</i> Climbing walls would cost Essence but not armor.) This effect lasts for a scene, and multiple strikes do not stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:50:55-07:00","id":963947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963313-lodge-of-the-seven-pyres#post963313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lodge Sacred Hunt allows your character to disrupt the prey spirit's protection from the host; by spending an Essence and successfully striking the Claimed (without causing damage), the Uratha causes the spirit to bleed a point of Essence per hour. This effect lasts for a number of hours equal to the Uratha's Primal Urge. In addition, during this time, the leaking Essence creates a trail of resonance that adds a one die bonus to attempt to track the Claimed. Multiple strikes will not increase the hemorrhaging of Essence, but will add to the length of time it is in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the two, I would definitely go with this one. I think it has use, but it isn't so powerful that it takes precedents over existing gifts. One potential bonus is the hemorrhaging essence could allow the pack to track the claimed from the Hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T20:29:13-07:00","id":964043,"title":"","content":"I think that first ability is so underpowered it's useless. For one thing, if you're attacking the creature in the first place why would it matter if it's loses Essence in an hour? And the attack doesn't even allow you to do damage. This is a rite of the Sacred Hunt, you're likely targeting this prey to begin with.<br /> <br /> Look at the Fighting Style Spiritual Blockage. One makes an attack with a -2 penalty, the damage is still done, and the target loses 1 to 2 Essence right there and then. And that involves some training, not binding your soul to the totem of a lodge and performing the ritual of the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> Then there's an added tracking ability, a one die bonus. But if you manage to bite the creature, again doing damage, you can taste it's blood. From there you can determine the creature's exact direction for a month. That's as a natural werewolf ability that costs nothing but a drop of the target's blood.<br /> <br /> I think you should only go with that first option if the lodge totem is Rank 2 and the lodge is very small and weak.<br /> <br /> The powerful option fits the game more, and fits the enemy they're fighting more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:57:39-07:00","id":964678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that first ability is so underpowered it's useless. For one thing, if you're attacking the creature in the first place why would it matter if it's loses Essence in an hour? And the attack doesn't even allow you to do damage. This is a rite of the Sacred Hunt, you're likely targeting this prey to begin with.<br /> . </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea of the weaker one was to make the spirit start bleeding Essence as it would without the host. I've never seen a Sacred Hunt before; I figured it would start with the pack IDing the claimed, someone sneaking up and doing the old Five Point Essence Bleed Technique punch, and then the merry chase as they run the weaking prey to ground. But, if I was a player, I would prefer something more potent. Still, will few examples to work from, I wasn't sure how to scale it. I may wind up with a bit of both. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it has use, but it isn't so powerful that it takes precedents over existing gifts. . </div> </div> </div>I think that is the challenge -- something potent enough to be useful, without necessarily stepping on the territory of gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:43:54-07:00","id":967660,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Lodge of the Seven Pyres (2E) </b></span><br /> <b>Deadliners, Skiptracers, <i>Imir Imkikidu</i></b><br /> <br /> There is a legendary boogyman among the Uratha. They call it the <i>Hisnimmuthim</i>, the Seven-Who-Are-One, the Dark Storm. Vampires have another name for it: VII. Every few years or decades, it descends on a city at nightfall. By dawn, all the vampires of the city are no more. Uratha who stay well away have described the attack as a force of nature, implacable and inescapable. Uratha who venture too close die, without exception. <br /> <br /> The Deadliners specialize in hunting Claimed, but ultimately, their goal is to take down the most powerful Spirit-Claimed in the world. One would expect the Storm Lords to be clamoring to join. In fact, the lodge is not well known at all. Membership is by invitation only, and all members have some connection, however tenuous, to VII. Perhaps the spiritual turmoil from a VII attack brought on her First Change. Or maybe he was hunting a vampire, only to lose the prey to a shadowy form of great power. And unlike many lodges, Seven Pyres is not limited to Uratha. Several vampires of the Hetkepu are members, for example \u2013 one of their number \u201ctamed\u201d the Lodge's totem, and VII\u2019s vengeance burned hottest against that bloodline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Seven are They!</b><br /> <br /> <i>Raising their evil heads, in the night shaking themselves, are they, evil searching out, are they,</i><br /> <i>Baleful are they, baleful are they, seven are they, seven are they, twice seven are they</i>! <i>May the spirits of heaven remember, may the spirits of earth remember.</i><br /> \u2013 <i>The Seven Evil Spirits</i>, translated by R.C.Thompson<br /> <br /> Though no one knows for certain, the prevailing thinking is that, somehow, a powerful spirit of darkness Claimed seven vampires at once. The beings known as VII probably originated in the Middle East, perhaps in the Golden Crescent. They are said to have first fought the vampires of Babylon, and slew most of the vampires on the Nile in 1103 BC. They were driven out of Rome with great losses in the 1st century BC. Since the 8th century, there have been scores of attacks in major population centers, with similar patterns: all (or nearly all) active vampires killed or missing, likewise any werewolves who might get in the way, and a <i>Hisil</i> in turmoil like a lakeshore in a boat's wake. They attack with tendrils of pure night striking out from their ebon forms, and their victims crumple or vanish in darkness. The Lodge has not yet divined a pattern in when or where VII attack. No pack has stood up to VII and lived. </td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>BOND</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> When trying to detect or track a spirit-Claimed, add a bonus equal to the spirits' Rank.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Gain knowledge or experience that moves them closer to the goal of finding and destroying the <i>Hisnimmuthim</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Except when an enemy has the drop on them (<i>i.e.</i>, strikes first) lodge members should always pause, assess and pick the most opportune time to strike \u2013 even if that means passing up easy shots. <br /> <br /> <b><u>SACRED HUNT</u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt allows your character to disrupt the prey spirit's connection with the host; by spending an Essence and successfully striking the Claimed, the Uratha forces the spirit to spend double the amount of Essence for any use of Influence; in addition, any Dread Power costs a point of Essence to use actively (<i>eg.,</i> Climbing walls would cost Essence but not armor.) This effect lasts for one scene and is not affected by multiple strikes. <br /> <br /> Additionally, the spirit loses its host's protection against Essence Bleed, and will lose a point of Essence per hour; during this time, the leaking Essence creates a trail of resonance that adds a one die bonus to attempt to track the Claimed. This effect lasts for a number of hours equal to the Uratha\u2019s Primal Urge. Multiple strikes will not increase the hemorrhaging of Essence, but will add to the length of time it is in effect.<br /> <br /> <b><u>TOOLS</u></b><br /> Lodge Members can purchase Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Stronghold. The lodge houses have rooms that no Claimed can enter without burning the spirit from flesh. They also contain small libraries of tomes, journals, and treatises related to their quarrry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Totem: Death Chooses When to Slay</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 10, Finesse 12, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>10<br /> <b>Essence:</b>25<br /> <b>Initiative:</b><br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 25<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 14<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Stealth \u2022\u2022\u2022, Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Vengeance \u2022<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Reaching, Materialize, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Ghost Eater, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Seek, Speed<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot instigate an attack without studying the prey first.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Any part of a ritually mummified hawk from Ancient Egypt.<br /> <b>Description: </b>A hulking owl that, in the darkness, is easy to overlook until the great glowing eyes are on you and its talons extend.<br /> <br /> <i>Death Chooses When To Slay</i> was an owl spirit haunting the Nile Valley. The peoples of ancient Egypt feared the owl as a death spirit and troubler of sleep. A fearsome hunter, <i>Death Chooses </i> often watched its target for hours before swooping in for a lethal strike. An undead priestess of Amun coaxed it into helping to guard the temple. Over generations it grew accustomed to its role as guardian and messenger, and warmed to its spirit-touched masters. Then, when VII destroyed most of the Kindred of Khem in one calamitous evening , the owl-spirit was retasked to hunt the Hisnimmuthim that slew so many. But the VII proved as ellusive as they were powerful.<br /> <br /> Over the next 3100 years, the spirit grew in power, and eventually discovered tools to assist it in its task: the Uratha. A couple of dozen werewolves search for news of VII and prepare themselves for the final showdown by hunting down Claimed.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:07:24-07:00","id":980803,"title":"","content":"It honestly feels a bit too broad for a Lodge's hunting refinement - it's just flat-out a Tribal favoured prey, which even the broadest of the Tribal Pillars refine down at least somewhat. I would narrow it down to specifically benefiting just against these weird VII Claimed (or possibly any 'vampire possession' type of prey situation - including vampires using Disciplines to possess others and Strix bodyjacking).<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso: &quot;The lodge houses have rooms that no Claimed can enter without burning the spirit from flesh.&quot; - this is a massive, massive power in terms of ramifications and implications, because you suddenly have that most prized and impossible of things - a deClaimer. If you can capture Claimed you can just throw them into the room and get the effect. The Storm Lords would literally kill for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:29:38-07:00","id":980820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963313-lodge-of-the-seven-pyres?p=980803#post980803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It honestly feels a bit too broad for a Lodge's hunting refinement - it's just flat-out a Tribal favoured prey, which even the broadest of the Tribal Pillars refine down at least somewhat. I would narrow it down to specifically benefiting just against these weird VII Claimed (or possibly any 'vampire possession' type of prey situation - including vampires using Disciplines to possess others and Strix bodyjacking).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. From the standpoint of my game, having it that specific would likely only useful once in a chronicle unless the pack was globe-trotting. VII (in my setting) is liable to manifest somewhere in the world every decade or so. And I've never used the Strix -- the game started before the revised edition came out. Picking up on Possession by Dominate might be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963313-lodge-of-the-seven-pyres?p=980803#post980803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso: &quot;The lodge houses have rooms that no Claimed can enter without burning the spirit from flesh.&quot; - this is a massive, massive power in terms of ramifications and implications, because you suddenly have that most prized and impossible of things - a deClaimer. If you can capture Claimed you can just throw them into the room and get the effect. The Storm Lords would literally kill for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was overstated, admittedly. The idea was like an invisible fence for dogs -- burns like hell and does damage at the threshold, but if you power your way through you're fine until you try to leave.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}